course: dictionary
lesson: 4126
title: Shining words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gleam can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing). As a verb it means to shine softly or brightly, often by reflecting light: «The polished car gleamed.» The car shines because it bounces the light back.
explain: As a noun, a gleam is a soft light or shine, or a small sign of a feeling or idea. «A gleam of hope» means a tiny bit of hope, not a light you can see. The words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Look at «a gleam in his eye». Nobody's eye is really glowing like a lamp. The phrase tells you the person has a clever or mischievous idea. Always ask what would fit, then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Gleam can be a verb (gleams, gleamed, gleaming) or a noun (a gleam, gleams).
fact: «Gleamed» means shone softly or brightly, often by reflecting light.
fact: «A gleam» means a soft light, or a small sign of a feeling or idea.
fact: «A gleam in his eye» often means someone has a clever or mischievous idea.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the river gleams and sparkles in the sun.
exercise: «The polished car gleamed.» What does gleamed mean? | Went very slowly | Made a loud crash | *Shone brightly by reflecting light | Was covered in mud
exercise: Ella says «a gleam of hope» means a big pile of hope. What does gleam mean here? | A dark cloud | A heavy load | *A small sign of hope | A loud shout
exercise: «He had a gleam in his eye as he thought of a plan.» What does this suggest? | He was very cold | He had lost his glasses | He was falling asleep | *He had a clever or mischievous idea
test: «The snow made the wood a gleaming carpet of faery.» Find and copy one word that means shining softly. | *gleaming | carpet | faery | wood
test: In «a gleaming carpet of faery», what does gleaming tell us about the snow? | It was made of wool | *It shone brightly | It was dirty and grey | It was quiet and hidden
exam: «A gleam of hope crossed her face.» Which meaning of gleam fits here? | To dig a hole | A loud bang | To run very fast | *A small sign of a feeling
